{
  "project": "cadi-alfa",
  "module": "game_state",
  "description": "Define el estado raíz del motor agregando estado del mundo, estado del protagonista y memoria del sistema.",
  "functions": [
    {
      "name": "new",
      "signature": "fn new() -> GameState",
      "description": "Construye un GameState con world_state, player_state y memory_state inicializados usando sus respectivos constructores.",
      "examples": [
        "GameState::new()"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tests": [
    "#[test] fn test_new_game_state_starts_with_zero_jornada() { let state = GameState::new(); assert_eq!(state.world.time.jornada_absoluta, 0); }",
    "#[test] fn test_new_game_state_starts_with_empty_memory_history() { let state = GameState::new(); assert!(state.memory.historial_eventos.is_empty()); }",
    "#[test] fn test_new_game_state_starts_with_empty_player_relations() { let state = GameState::new(); assert!(state.player.relaciones.is_empty()); }"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    "serde"
  ],
  "notes": "Implementar `GameState` como struct público con campos `world: WorldState`, `player: PlayerState` y `memory: MemoryState`. Usar `#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, Default)]` y delegar la inicialización a los constructores de los subtipos. Evitar campos o lógica adicional no especificada."
}
